+### Engine A â€” Claude Code `/goal` (attended hands-free; not a background job)
.loop/driver.log:5901: trailing whitespace.
+
.loop/driver.log:5902: trailing whitespace.
+**Hard prerequisites â€” confirm all of these with the user before handing over
.loop/driver.log:5903: trailing whitespace.
+the command; if any fails, or the real intent is unattended, recommend Engine B
.loop/driver.log:5904: trailing whitespace.
+instead:**
.loop/driver.log:5905: trailing whitespace.
+
.loop/driver.log:5906: trailing whitespace.
+1. Claude Code â‰¥ v2.1.139, workspace trust dialog accepted, hooks enabled.
.loop/driver.log:5907: trailing whitespace.
+2. **Auto mode ON** (tool calls auto-approved). Without it the loop halts at
.loop/driver.log:5908: trailing whitespace.
+   the first permission prompt. This is a hard precondition, not an
.loop/driver.log:5909: trailing whitespace.
+   optimization.
.loop/driver.log:5910: trailing whitespace.
+3. **The session stays open for the whole run.** `/goal` advances **exactly one
.loop/driver.log:5911: trailing whitespace.
+   turn per Stop-hook evaluation**, and only in a live session. It is not a
.loop/driver.log:5912: trailing whitespace.
+   scheduler, not a daemon, not background work. Closing the client, sleeping
.loop/driver.log:5913: trailing whitespace.
+   the laptop, or losing the session stops the crank (a still-active goal is
.loop/driver.log:5914: trailing whitespace.
+=== execution 181-360 ===
.loop/driver.log:5915: trailing whitespace.
